---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Article from '../components/Article.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

// Text supplied by the client: "Piran_Builders_Website_Privacy_Policy.pdf", last updated 12 November 2026.
// Keep it word for word; when the client sends a new version, replace the text and the date together.
const mail = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${site.legalName} collects, uses, stores and protects your personal information under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.`}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy." lede="Privacy Policy & UK GDPR Data Protection Notice: how we collect, use, store and protect your personal information." image="/frames/lg/0040.webp" crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} />
  <Article updated="Last updated: 12 November 2026">
    <div class="legal">
      <dl class="legal-facts">
        <div><dt>Data Controller</dt><dd>{site.legalName} (England &amp; Wales)</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Company Reg. No.</dt><dd>{site.companyNumber}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Registered Office</dt><dd>{site.registeredOffice}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Operational Base</dt><dd>Coventry, United Kingdom</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Privacy Contact</dt><dd><a href={mail}>{site.email}</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Telephone / WhatsApp</dt><dd><a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> | Mobile &amp; WhatsApp <a href={site.mobileHref}>{site.mobile}</a> | piranbuilders.co.uk</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Last Updated</dt><dd>12 November 2026</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Applicable Law</dt><dd>UK GDPR &amp; Data Protection Act 2018</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <p class="legal-intro"><strong>Piran Builders Ltd</strong> (“we,” “our,” or “us”) is committed to protecting and respecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and safeguard your personal data when you visit <strong>piranbuilders.co.uk</strong>, request a free consultation or quotation, contact us via phone, email, or WhatsApp, engage our building services, or apply to join our team. We process all personal data in strict compliance with the <strong>UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR)</strong> and the <strong>Data Protection Act 2018</strong>.</p>

      <h2>1. Personal Data We Collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect and process the following categories of personal information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiry &amp; Quote Information:</strong> Your full name, email address, telephone/WhatsApp number, property address and postcode, selected trade service, and project details submitted via our website quote form, phone calls, emails, or WhatsApp messages.</li>
        <li><strong>Contract &amp; Project Records:</strong> Site survey notes, architectural drawings, written quotations, variation agreements, payment records, invoices, Building Control/compliance certificates, and workmanship guarantee documentation.</li>
        <li><strong>Project Photography (Opt-In Only):</strong> Photographs or short videos of completed building works, collected and published strictly where you have provided explicit written opt-in consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Recruitment &amp; Subcontractor Information:</strong> Contact details, CVs, trade qualifications (e.g., CSCS, Gas Safe, NICEIC), insurance certificates, and work history if you apply for employment or subcontractor roles.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical &amp; Usage Data:</strong> Basic browser type, device information, IP address, and essential website security logs collected automatically when you browse <strong>piranbuilders.co.uk</strong>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How and Why We Use Your Data (Lawful Bases)</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR, we only process your personal data when we have a valid lawful basis to do so:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Purpose of Processing</th><th scope="col">Categories of Data Used</th><th scope="col">UK GDPR Lawful Basis</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Responding to enquiries, arranging free consultations, and preparing written quotations</td><td data-label="Categories of Data Used">Name, email, phone number, property location, project description</td><td data-label="UK GDPR Lawful Basis">Steps prior to entering into a contract / Legitimate interests</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Delivering construction, renovation, and trade services, managing schedules, and invoicing</td><td data-label="Categories of Data Used">Contact details, site address, payment and contract records</td><td data-label="UK GDPR Lawful Basis">Performance of a contract</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Honouring 12-month workmanship and 6-month plastering guarantees</td><td data-label="Categories of Data Used">Client contact details, completion dates, scope of works</td><td data-label="UK GDPR Lawful Basis">Performance of a contract / Legal obligation</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Showcasing completed project photography on our website or social media</td><td data-label="Categories of Data Used">Anonymised property/workmanship photos (no personal identifiers)</td><td data-label="UK GDPR Lawful Basis">Explicit consent (Written Opt-In)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reviewing job and subcontractor applications</td><td data-label="Categories of Data Used">Name, contact details, CV, trade certifications, insurance records</td><td data-label="UK GDPR Lawful Basis">Steps prior to entering into a contract</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Maintaining accounting, tax (HMRC), health &amp; safety, and insurance compliance records</td><td data-label="Categories of Data Used">Invoices, receipts, contracts, site safety &amp; compliance certificates</td><td data-label="UK GDPR Lawful Basis">Legal obligation</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>3. Sharing Your Personal Data &amp; International Transfers</h2>
      <p>We <strong>never</strong> sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third parties for marketing purposes. We only share personal data where strictly necessary to deliver your project or operate our business lawfully:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Trusted Tradespeople &amp; Subcontractors:</strong> Qualified specialist trades (such as NICEIC registered electricians or Gas Safe engineers) working on your project under strict confidentiality and data protection obligations.</li>
        <li><strong>Material Suppliers &amp; Delivery Partners:</strong> Your name, contact number, and site delivery address where direct-to-site delivery of building materials, windows, kitchens, or fixtures is required.</li>
        <li><strong>Professional &amp; Regulatory Bodies:</strong> Accountants, insurers, Building Control inspectors, certification schemes, or legal advisers where required for statutory compliance, warranties, or insurance cover.</li>
        <li><strong>Communication, Cloud &amp; IT Providers:</strong> Website hosting, email, and messaging platforms (including WhatsApp when you choose to message us via that channel). Where service providers store or process data outside the UK (such as in the United States), we ensure transfers are protected by valid UK GDPR safeguards, including the <strong>UK-US Data Bridge</strong> or the <strong>UK International Data Transfer Agreement (IDTA)</strong>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Data Retention Periods</h2>
      <p>We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected and to meet legal, accounting, and insurance requirements:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Quote Enquiries (Not Proceeding):</strong> Retained for up to <strong>12 months</strong> in case you decide to revisit your project, unless you ask us to delete them sooner.</li>
        <li><strong>Completed Projects &amp; Financial Records:</strong> Retained for <strong>6 to 7 years</strong> following project completion to comply with HMRC accounting laws, limitation periods for contractual claims, warranty obligations, and insurance requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Recruitment &amp; Subcontractor Enquiries:</strong> Unsuccessful applications are retained for up to <strong>6 months</strong> unless you consent to longer retention.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Data Security</h2>
      <p>We implement appropriate technical and organisational security measures—including encrypted website connections (HTTPS/SSL), strong password and two-factor authentication (2FA) controls, encrypted device storage, and restricted staff access—to protect your personal data against unauthorised access, accidental loss, alteration, or disclosure.</p>

      <h2>6. Cookies &amp; External Links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> Our website (<strong>piranbuilders.co.uk</strong>) uses essential functional cookies necessary for core site navigation, security, and enquiry form submission. If we introduce any non-essential analytics or marketing cookies, we will request your explicit cookie consent via a banner before activating them. You can also manage or block cookies through your browser settings at any time.</li>
        <li><strong>Third-Party Links:</strong> Our website may include links to external platforms such as WhatsApp, Facebook, or Instagram. Once you leave <strong>piranbuilders.co.uk</strong>, those platforms are governed by their own respective privacy policies.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Your Rights Under UK GDPR</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Right of Access:</strong> Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you (Subject Access Request).</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> Ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete personal information.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Erasure (“Right to be Forgotten”):</strong> Request deletion of your personal data where there is no legal or contractual reason for us to continue holding it.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Restrict or Object:</strong> Object to or request restriction of processing based on legitimate interests, or withdraw consent where processing relies on consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Data Portability:</strong> Request the transfer of your data in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format where applicable.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout">
        <p class="callout-title">How to exercise your rights or make a data complaint</p>
        <p>To exercise any of your UK GDPR rights, please email <a href={mail}><strong>{site.email}</strong></a> or call <a href={site.phoneHref}><strong>{site.phone}</strong></a>. We will respond within one calendar month. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the UK supervisory authority, the <strong>Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO)</strong>, at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>ico.org.uk</strong></a> or by calling 0303 123 1113 if you are unhappy with how we have handled your data.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>8. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in our business operations or UK legal requirements. The latest version will always be published on <strong>piranbuilders.co.uk</strong> with an updated effective date.</p>
    </div>
  </Article>
</Base>
